{"title":"Marketing Science: Multinomial Logit & Latent Class Analysis","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Marketing Science: Multinomial Logit & Latent Class Analysis","author":"Shuhei Kuwabara","date":"2025-11-13","categories":["R","Marketing","Statistics"],"image":"latent.jpg","description":"Segmentation and brand choice analysis using Latent Class Models.","resources":["report.qmd","data/chapter_06_choice.csv"]},"headingText":"Project Overview","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n\nThis project investigates consumer brand choice behavior using **Multinomial Logit** and **Latent Class Analysis (LCA)**. The analysis focuses on identifying distinct consumer segments to optimize pricing strategies and understand market heterogeneity.\n\n\n## Access the Files\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"file-list-group\">\n  \n  <a href=\"report.html\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-lines\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">View Full Report</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Web-based interactive report with visualizations.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"report.qmd\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Source Code (.qmd)</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Reproducible source code for this analysis.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"data/chapter_06_choice.csv\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-download\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Download Dataset</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Original CSV data file.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"original.pdf\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-pdf\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Original Report (PDF)</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Original submission in Japanese.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n</div>\n```\n\n## Methodology\nThis analysis moves beyond aggregate preferences by employing **Latent Class Analysis (LCA)** to uncover hidden segments within the consumer population.\n\n### 1. Baseline Modeling (Multinomial Logit)\nInitially, a standard Multinomial Logit (MNL) model was fitted to establish baseline average effects.\n\nResult: Price has a significant negative effect (-0.37), and feature ads have a positive effect (+0.49) on brand choice across the aggregate population.\n\n### 2. Identifying Heterogeneity (LCA)\n\nTo capture market heterogeneity, I fitted Finite Mixture Models using the flexmix package, testing from k=1 to k=6 classes.\n\nModel Selection: Based on the Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC) and model interpretability, a 4-class model was selected.\n\n\n\n##  Tech Stack\n\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">R</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">Multinomial Logit</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">Latent Class Analysis</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">tidyverse</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">mlogit</span>","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis project investigates consumer brand choice behavior using **Multinomial Logit** and **Latent Class Analysis (LCA)**. The analysis focuses on identifying distinct consumer segments to optimize pricing strategies and understand market heterogeneity.\n\n\n## Access the Files\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"file-list-group\">\n  \n  <a href=\"report.html\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-lines\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">View Full Report</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Web-based interactive report with visualizations.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"report.qmd\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-code\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Source Code (.qmd)</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Reproducible source code for this analysis.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"data/chapter_06_choice.csv\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-download\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Download Dataset</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Original CSV data file.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n  <a href=\"original.pdf\" class=\"file-list-item\">\n    <div class=\"file-list-icon\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-file-pdf\"></i></div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-content\">\n      <span class=\"file-list-title\">Original Report (PDF)</span>\n      <span class=\"file-list-desc\">Original submission in Japanese.</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"file-list-arrow\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right\"></i></div>\n  </a>\n\n</div>\n```\n\n## Methodology\nThis analysis moves beyond aggregate preferences by employing **Latent Class Analysis (LCA)** to uncover hidden segments within the consumer population.\n\n### 1. Baseline Modeling (Multinomial Logit)\nInitially, a standard Multinomial Logit (MNL) model was fitted to establish baseline average effects.\n\nResult: Price has a significant negative effect (-0.37), and feature ads have a positive effect (+0.49) on brand choice across the aggregate population.\n\n### 2. Identifying Heterogeneity (LCA)\n\nTo capture market heterogeneity, I fitted Finite Mixture Models using the flexmix package, testing from k=1 to k=6 classes.\n\nModel Selection: Based on the Bayesian Information Criterion (BIC) and model interpretability, a 4-class model was selected.\n\n\n\n##  Tech Stack\n\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">R</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">Multinomial Logit</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">Latent Class Analysis</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">tidyverse</span>\n<span class=\"tech-badge\">mlogit</span>"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":true,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":false,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":